# Evidence belongs to a run, not to the source tree.
#
# Every directory under artifacts/ is one invocation: its manifest, its
# events, its measurements, its defects and its summary. They are
# generated, they can be large, and an endurance run writes tens of
# thousands of event lines - none of which belongs in version control.
#
# WHAT TO DO WITH A RESULT THAT MATTERS. Copy the run directory out of
# here and attach it to the defect or the commit that cites it. A number
# quoted in a report with no run id behind it is an opinion; a run id
# with no archived directory behind it is a broken reference.
artifacts/

# The layer-gate ledger: which tests have passed on REAL hardware, on
# THIS bench. Machine-specific by definition - another machine's ledger
# would open gates here that nothing on this bench has earned.
ledger.json

# A bench profile names one physical instrument: its USB serial number,
# its device path, its operator. Copy profile.example.json and keep the
# copy local. The example itself IS tracked.
configuration/*.json
!configuration/profile.example.json
